17: **Q4 — wrong dispositions.** (1) The D1 lean — a rule, not a row; overturned above. (2) **F15 as recorded.** Kimi/codex are right the "UB evaluates as `>> 0`" rationale is argued, host-dependent and unmeasured — but everyone, me included, missed the sharper fact: pre-fix `tmp` was `uint64_t`, so `tmp >> 32` at sh=0 was DEFINED and the `sh ?` guard was redundant; the fix narrows `tmp` to `uint32_t`, making that shift UB and the guard LOAD-BEARING for definedness. "Predates the fix, not-a-gap" is therefore a wrong record: the fix changed the guard's status. No row can be built (the mutant is host-equivalent by construction if it is equivalent at all), so this is a record correction plus one named leg (`R_NOGUARD`, predicted 28/28) — non-blocking, because a red would only relabel it "host-dependent equivalent". (3) F12's exclusive list — already corrected to 0, 8, 24, 40. (4) Minor: F5's label reads as EQUIVALENT once the reason is read (`:318-322` assigns then exits on nonzero — verified), which is what the probe already says; ollama-kimi's wording point only. **Not wrong:** F4 (the self-doubt was misplaced — M5's 28/30 signature IS the two-way measurement); D_NO_MERGE (SCORES lists four failures: 25/29, settled by reading); D_NOCIRC (glm's "defined arithmetic" account is refuted by the loop's own structure — with `mb == end` and unmasked `m++`, termination needs `m` to wrap the int, so the POSTTABLE's slow-circular account is the coherent one; minimax's "below commit threshold" is an invented threshold on a UB leg the PRETABLE flagged "record, do not fit").
