5233: # `#526` (xscaleinten): reading the i80321 interrupt-enable register ended the emulator — AFTER the model had already loaded the correct value into the destination register
5234: 
5235: **THE DEFECT.** `arm_coproc_i80321_6()` — coprocessor 6 on `-E iq80321` (and Iyonix), installed by
5236: `machine_iq80321.c` — handles `crm 0 / crn 0` as the interrupt-enable register.  Its load arm read:
5237: 
5238: ```c
5239: cpu->cd.arm.r[rd] = cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten;
5240: fatal("TODO: XScale read from inten?\n");
5241: exit(1);
5242: ```
5243: 
5244: **The destination received the modelled value and the host process then died.**  The register is fully
5245: modelled in both directions: the store arm writes the same field, and `dev_i80321.c` consumes it
5246: (`d->enable = &cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten`).  A guest reading back its own interrupt enables — which is
5247: what firmware does — ended the emulator.
5248: 
5249: **THE SIBLING IN THE SAME SWITCH IS THE WARRANT.**  `crn 4` (isteer) has the identical load/store
5250: shape and its read carries no diagnostic and no exit.  `crn 0`'s kill is the switch's outlier —
5251: upstream residue, the exit the author reached while developing, not a policy.
5252: 
5253: **THE FIX — ACCEPT (member 4 of the option set).**  Delete the two lines; keep the value.  No latch
5254: and no announce: the read is implemented, so a bounded "unimplemented" message would be a wrong
5255: record in product code.  The write arm, and the three kills this round RETAINS in the same handler —
5256: the isteer non-zero write, the isrc write (`TODO: XScale int ack?`) and the unknown-tuple exit — are
5257: untouched and rowed as controls.  Every seat that read the source in two passes upheld ACCEPT.
5258: 
5259: **THE WITNESS, and one thing it does NOT establish.**  Rung 3, cold debugger, unmodified in-tree
5260: `iq80321`: `regress/artifacts/xscaleinten/agy_xscale_witness_20260911.py`, committed build **11/26**,
5261: fix **26/26** (`witness_committed.out`, `witness_fix.out`).  **Test-first ORDER is not established by
5262: these artifacts**: `witness_fix.out` carries the EARLIER mtime (`02:20:10` against `02:20:23`), and
5263: nothing records that the committed leg was run before the edit.  What IS established, three times, is
5264: that the committed source reproduces the death from a clean rebuild: every kill table's HEAD leg
5265: (11/26, 12/29, 12/30).  *Recorded as a reproducible pre-fix measurement, not as test-first.*
5266: 
5267: ## The detector — `regress/xscale_inten_probe.py`, 30 rows, `gate_arm.sh` pin 30
5268: 
5269: Promoted from the witness with codex's repairs (`codex_promote_20260912b.txt`, answered after the
5270: cybersecurity filter refused the first wording): a RESULT/CONTROL/DONE protocol, captured values kept
5271: when a later step dies with unreached rows reported **BLOCKED** (not failed, not passed), a non-zero
5272: exit on any non-passing row, and three new rows — `D_OP1` (read with opcode1 = 1),
5273: `INTEN_WRITE_PRESERVES_ISTEER`, and `D_CRM1_TMR0` (crm isolation at crn 0).  Pass 2 added the
5274: thirtieth, `RD0_ALLONES`.  The header carries a CONTRACT and a NOT COVERED list (clause (e)).
5275: 
5276: | table | instrument | legs | result |
5277: |---|---|---|---|
5278: | 1 `killtable_20260911/` | witness, 26 rows | 7 | M1 23, M5 25, M_OPCODE2 19, M_NREAD 19, M_RD15 25 — all killed |
5279: | 2 `killtable2_20260912/` | 29 rows | 10 | 9 on prediction; HEAD predicted 13/29, measured 12/29 (a BLOCKED row counted as a pass in the prediction's arithmetic) |
5280: | 3 `killtable3_20260912/` | 30 rows | 12 | **12 on prediction**; BASE 30/30, HEAD 12/30, every mutant killed |
