24434: 
24435: #### `qhmbphasestops` (HIGH, filed by #558) -- An MB89352 data-register access, with a transfer object and a nonzero count, in a phase unsupported for the access direction stops the emulated CPU
24436: SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :169 (DREG read, phase outside DATAIN/STAT/MSGIN) and :235 (DREG write, phase outside DATAOUT/CMD).  :290 (the end-of-write default:) is UNREACHABLE: the first switch returns only for unsupported phases, and DATAOUT/CMD break, reach the second switch with no intervening phase change, and exhaust its supported cases.  PREREQUISITES: every DREG helper call needs a NONZERO count before decrement (a zero-count access only warns) and these guards additionally need a transfer object -- 'unconditional' means independent of the abort flag, nothing more.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): SCMD/PCTL give the guest control of the phase.  FIX SHAPE: keep the CPU running while KEEPING the helper's early return (:170 / :236) -- the treatment #186 gave the XFR command at :507.
24437: #### `qhmbunimplstops` (HIGH, filed by #558) -- An MB89352 access with a non-byte length, an unhandled SCMD write, or the EXBF register stops the emulated CPU while mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff is fixed true
24438: SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :312 (len != 1: a halfword or word callback access), :533 (an SCMD WRITE outside {0x00, 0x20, 0x84, 0x8c, 0xc0} unless bit 0x10 rewrites it to BUS_REL -- an SCMD read does not execute this switch), and EXBF, register index 15: WRITE logging at :676 and READ logging at :683 converge on the ONE assignment at :690.  All gated by const bool mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff = true (:61), so live; the shared fixed-true policy is what groups them.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): those accesses from the guest's register interface.  FIX SHAPE: the warning branch the flag already selects; clearing the flag leaves all five live unconditional DREG assignments (:146, :169, :176, :235, :242; :290 is dead) intact.  NOT mb89352halt's stop: that dropped row's record names the disk dispatcher's CDB default: and the controller's status-length guard, not :533.
24439: #### `qhmbbufendstops` (HIGH, filed by #558) -- An MB89352 data-register access at or past the end of the selected buffer, in a phase supported for the access direction, stops the emulated CPU
24440: SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :176 (DREG read, transfer_bufpos >= len against the selected DATAIN, STAT or MSGIN buffer -- read completion changes phase WITHOUT resetting the cursor, so a subsequent nonempty buffer can meet this guard, not only the original DATAIN buffer) and :242 (DREG write: reachable through empty or unprepared outgoing-buffer states; an exact fill runs completion and can change phase so a further write reaches :235 instead).  PREREQUISITES: a transfer object and a nonzero count, as for the phase guards (the count prerequisite applies to every DREG helper call; the :146 stop is the case with NO transfer object).  CARRIERS OF THE REST: b120 carries the unknown-CDB producer omission and its empty-status consequence; this row's residual is every OTHER empty-buffer path and every nonempty-buffer case.  FIX SHAPE: keep the bounds protection and refuse the access or handle phase completion -- removing the guard exposes the indexed accesses at :180 / :246 -- a CONTROLLER fix; b120 remains the PRODUCER fix.
